<title>USA: Cornell Corrections Inc turns Q1 profit.</title>
<headline>Cornell Corrections Inc turns Q1 profit.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>3 months ended March 31,</p>
<p>							     1997	1996</p>
<p> Revenues						$13,200   $5,453</p>
<p> Operating expenses				   10,797    4,562</p>
<p> Depreciation and amortization			 448	237</p>
<p> General and administrative expenses	     1,069	714</p>
<p> Income (loss) from operations			 886     (60)</p>
<p> Interest expense, net				    52	201</p>
<p> Income (loss) before income taxes		   834    (261)</p>
<p> Net income (loss)					 500    (261)</p>
<p> Earnings (loss) per share			    0.07   (0.07)</p>
<p> Number of shares used to compute EPS	    7,106    3,522</p>
<p> Contracted beds in operation (end of period)  3,537    1,251</p>
<p> Average occupancy(A)				  94.7%    94.0%</p>
<p>			  (000's except per share amounts)</p>
<p>(A)  Occupancy percentages are based on contracted beds in operation.</p>
<p>Since certain facilities have design capacities that exceed contract capacities, occupancy percentages can exceed 100% of contracted capacity.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
